      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2: a contributor's second create for the same key replaces the first (version 2 of the first record, one command.committed event and one outcome naming it, creator and updater the contributor); the second form's id is never created; the dry run names the entry it replaces; a replay returns the stored outcome",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2: a create with the values the entry already holds is 422 unchanged (dry run too): nothing written, the claim released, so the same key is judged again later",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2 x D7: two creators with the same key keep two entries; neither create (nor the dry run) touches the other's (fails under bypass)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2 x D7: a reviewer's own create never matches a contributor's entry, although the reviewer reads every entry (fails under bypass)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2: the reviewer's listing counts one entry per creator per key (Ben's four answers to item one are one record)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3: an answer while the item is open and inside its window commits; after the reviewer's close it is 422 requirement_not_met (dry run too) and nothing is written; a contributor cannot reopen; the reviewer's reopen re-stamps opened_at and answers are accepted again (replacing the entry)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3: a reference to a record that does not exist, to a record of another collection or to an id outside the work is the uniform 404 (commit and dry run), never requirement_not_met",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3 now: 31 s after the post (the database's clock) an open item refuses answers with requirement_not_met (dry run too), its state still open; the reviewer's reopen (state unchanged) re-stamps opened_at and answers are accepted again",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3 set_now on a contributor's create: checked_at is the transaction's instant (the outcome's committed_at)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3 x D7: a via reference into another member's own list is the uniform 404 (commit and dry run); the creator and a reviewer resolve it (fails under bypass)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C3 now: `closes_at > now` accepts a check-in before the deadline and refuses one at it (requirement_not_met, dry run too); a member's close of their own session refuses their next check-in",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "APP-205: a contributor's respond form offers every readable item newest commit first, the current (most recently touched) item preselected and labelled by its prompt; the post form's stamped opened_at is read-only; the selection posted through the native form's parse commits a typed reference storage accepts",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "APP-205 x D7: a picker over an own list offers only the records the member may read (a contributor their own, a reviewer every member's); a member who can read none gets the disabled picker (fails under bypass)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "name": "C2 race: 25 simultaneous creates by one creator for one key leave exactly one entry whose state is one of the submitted states; its 18 commits have versions 1..18 and every outcome names it; the other 7 were 422 unchanged; no other requested id exists (0 admission refusals, each resent with its key)",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
